                          "text":  "I am the youngest one out here. I launched in January 2006, faster than anything had ever left Earth, on my way to the last unexplored planet. Seven months later, astronomers decided Pluto should be called a dwarf planet instead. I kept going. A world is a world.\n\nJupiter gave me a push in 2007. After that I mostly slept, year after year, waking up now and then to check that everything still worked.",
